 populous city of Niigata Prefecture, and one of the cities designated by government ordinance of Japan, located in the Chūbu region of Japan. It is the most populous city on the west coast of Honshu, and the second most populous city in the Chūbu region after Nagoya. It faces the Sea of Japan and Sado Island. As of 1 September 2022, the city had an estimated population of 779,049, and a population density of 1,072 persons per km2. The total area is 726.45 square kilometres (280.48 sq mi). Greater Niigata, the Niigata Metropolitan Employment Area, has a GDP of US$43.3 billion as of 2010.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Niigata_from_Bandaijima_Building_20200906_P4.jpg/330px-Niigata_from_Bandaijima_Building_20200906_P4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niigata_(city)"},"twins":["Q959","Q135744","Q4454","Q7769","Q12191","Q42956","Q128147"],"climate":{"temp":[5,4.8,6.7,10.5,15.5,20,24,26.2,23.2,18.1,12.9,7.8],"rain":[166,105,107,95,85,113,213,145,141,151,168,215],"cloud":[89,85,80,74,72,79,82,72,75,75,78,87]},"land":true}